        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: show auto-detected provider plans and billing",
        "body": "Closes #100494\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex). I reviewed and understand the implementation.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's Usage page analyzes session token cost but does not show the provider-side plan, quota, balance, spend, or budget facts that determine whether an account can keep running. Provider usage support also depended on a core provider list, so provider plugins could not opt into the complete usage workflow themselves.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a provider-neutral billing model and a manifest-scoped `contracts.usageProviders` contract. Enabled provider plugins that declare the provider id and implement both usage-auth and usage-snapshot hooks are discovered automatically without importing unrelated provider runtimes.\n\nThe implementation follows the usage/cost model in [CodexBar main at `b43a0ef6`](https://github.com/steipete/codexbar/tree/b43a0ef645abc5d7c20d4f700932ac4d4b470ccf), adapted to OpenClaw's plugin ownership boundaries. It enriches Anthropic, Codex/OpenAI, DeepSeek, and ClawRouter; adds provider-owned [OpenRouter credits/key](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/limits/) and [Venice balance](https://docs.venice.ai/api-reference/endpoint/billing/balance) collection; and keeps provider billing separate from OpenClaw's own session-cost calculations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can see configured provider plans, resettable quota windows, balances, spend, and budgets in the Control UI Usage page and text status surfaces. New provider plugins can participate by declaring one manifest contract and implementing the two existing usage hooks; no core allowlist edit is required.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwt944qxsg7ja9e8wgcr7v1d`: exact-head `pnpm check:changed` passed in 9m56s.\n- Exact-head `pnpm test:contracts`: 1,274 tests passed.\n- Exact-head `pnpm build`: passed, including plugin SDK exports and production Control UI build.\n- Exact-head Chromium Usage E2E: provider cards rendered from a real mocked Gateway `usage.status` request; session-cost controls remained functional.\n- Focused provider/runtime/status suites: 242 tests passed; contract-owner regression suite: 124 tests passed.\n- Fresh autoreview: clean after addressing recurring limits, BYOK accounting, minor currency units, partial endpoint failures, malformed payloads, negative balances, zero-dollar limits, billing-only status output, and manifest-scoped discovery.\n- Live unauthenticated probes reached OpenRouter credits/key and Venice balance endpoints and returned HTTP 401. Authenticated billing proof was not available because the trusted Testbox had no OpenRouter or Venice credential; official response shapes are covered by bounded parser tests.\n\n### Before\n\n![Before: session cost analysis without provider billing cards](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d4597b2-c7df-4f61-baed-4fa96522a784)\n\n### After\n\n![After: provider plans and billing cards above session analysis](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/500627b0-f3ce-4d5a-b3bc-7d2b459c0725)\n",
